  "solution": "The logic followed here is,\n\n**Logic: Second no. = [(First no.) × (Third no.) × (7)]**\n\n**(8, 280, 5)** →\n\n⇒ ( 8 × 5 × 7)\n\n⇒ (40 × 7) = 280\n\n**(11, 308, 4)** →\n\n⇒ ( 11 × 4 × 7)\n\n⇒ (44 × 7) = 308\n\nChecking all the given options:\n\n1. (6, 370, 9)\n\n⇒ ( 6 × 9 × 7)\n\n⇒ (54 × 7) = 378\n\n2. (5, 270, 9)\n\n⇒ ( 5 × 9 × 7)\n\n⇒ (45 × 7) = 315\n\n**3. (13, 637, 7)**\n\n**⇒ ( 13 × 7 × 7)**\n\n**⇒ (91 × 7) = 637**\n\n4. (11, 440, 5)\n\n⇒ ( 11 × 5 × 7)\n\n⇒ (55 × 7) = 385\n\nHere, (13, 637, 7) shows a similar relation to the given set of numbers.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"**(13, 637, 7)**\".",
